IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc1-s25-reports.l4 -- Part I (General), sections 25.2 to 25.4: the report of a public officer, the annual report of a competent authority, and the written notification of a person
-- whose property was lost or seriously damaged. The duties are encoded twice, as the brief asks: as regulative rules (PARTY ... MUST ...), which are run with #TRACE, and as decision functions over the facts,
-- which are asserted (a regulative outcome cannot be asserted on the stable binary: see NOTES.md, "What the stable binary does not accept").
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- The core `Party` has no constructor for a senior official (section 25.1(1)) or a competent authority, so this module declares its own actor type under its section label (NEEDS-CORE.md records the constructors wanted).
-- The text gives no number of days for "as soon as is feasible" or "without delay"; none is invented: those duties have no WITHIN. The one period the text states, "no later than one year after the commission" (25.4(1)),
-- is WITHIN 1 on a clock that counts YEARS from the commission.

§ `Section 25.2 -- Public officer to file report`

-- src:702 | Public officer to file report
-- src:703 | 25.2 Every public officer who commits an act or omission — or directs the commission by another person of an act or omission — under paragraph 25.1(9)(a) or (b) shall, as soon as is feasible after the commission of the act or omission, file a written report with the appropriate senior official describing the act or omission.
@ref s 25.2 (src:702-703)
DECLARE `s 25.2 the person who bears the duty` IS ONE OF
    `s 25.2 a public officer`
    `s 25.2 a senior official`
    `s 25.2 a competent authority`

DECLARE `s 25.2 the act the duty is to do` IS ONE OF
    `s 25.2 file a written report with the appropriate senior official describing the act or omission`
    `s 25.3 publish or otherwise make available to the public the annual report for the previous year`
    `s 25.4 notify in writing the person whose property was lost or seriously damaged`
    `s 25.1(6) notify the competent authority of the designation`

@ref s 25.2 (src:703-703)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 25.2 the person who bears the duty` `s 25.2 the act the duty is to do`
`s 25.2 the duty of the public officer to file a written report` MEANS
    PARTY `s 25.2 a public officer`
    MUST `s 25.2 file a written report with the appropriate senior official describing the act or omission`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the public officer did not file a written report with the appropriate senior official as soon as was feasible after the act or omission"

@ref s 25.2 (src:703-703)
GIVEN `the public officer commits an act or omission, or directs the commission by another person of an act or omission, under paragraph 25.1(9)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25.2 the public officer is required to file a written report with the appropriate senior official` MEANS
    IF `the public officer commits an act or omission, or directs the commission by another person of an act or omission, under paragraph 25.1(9)(a) or (b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every public officer who commits an act or omission — or directs the commission by another person of an act or omission — under paragraph 25.1(9)(a) or (b)"

§ `Section 25.3 -- Annual report`

-- src:704 | Annual report
-- src:705 | 25.3 (1) Every competent authority shall publish or otherwise make available to the public an annual report for the previous year that includes, in respect of public officers and senior officials designated by the competent authority,
-- src:706 | (a) the number of designations made under subsection 25.1(6) by the senior officials;
-- src:707 | (b) the number of authorizations made under paragraph 25.1(9)(a) by the senior officials;
-- src:708 | (c) the number of times that acts and omissions were committed in accordance with paragraph 25.1(9)(b) by the public officers;
-- src:709 | (d) the nature of the conduct being investigated when the designations referred to in paragraph (a) or the authorizations referred to in paragraph (b) were made or when the acts or omissions referred to in paragraph (c) were committed; and
-- src:710 | (e) the nature of the acts or omissions committed under the designations referred to in paragraph (a), under the authorizations referred to in paragraph (b) and in the manner described in paragraph (c).
@ref s 25.3(1) (src:704-710)
DECLARE `s 25.3(1) the item` IS ONE OF
    `s 25.3(1)(a) the number of designations made under subsection 25.1(6) by the senior officials`
    `s 25.3(1)(b) the number of authorizations made under paragraph 25.1(9)(a) by the senior officials`
    `s 25.3(1)(c) the number of times that acts and omissions were committed in accordance with paragraph 25.1(9)(b) by the public officers`
    `s 25.3(1)(d) the nature of the conduct being investigated when the designations referred to in paragraph (a) or the authorizations referred to in paragraph (b) were made or when the acts or omissions referred to in paragraph (c) were committed`
    `s 25.3(1)(e) the nature of the acts or omissions committed under the designations referred to in paragraph (a), under the authorizations referred to in paragraph (b) and in the manner described in paragraph (c)`
    `s 25.3(1) another item`

@ref s 25.3(1) (src:704-705)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 25.2 the person who bears the duty` `s 25.2 the act the duty is to do`
`s 25.3(1) the duty of the competent authority to publish an annual report` MEANS
    PARTY `s 25.2 a competent authority`
    MUST `s 25.3 publish or otherwise make available to the public the annual report for the previous year`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the competent authority did not publish or otherwise make available to the public an annual report for the previous year"

@ref s 25.3(1) (src:704-705)
GIVEN `the person is a competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25.3(1) the competent authority is required to publish or otherwise make available to the public an annual report for the previous year` MEANS
    IF `the person is a competent authority`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every competent authority shall publish or otherwise make available to the public an annual report"

@ref s 25.3(1) (src:706-710)
GIVEN item IS A `s 25.3(1) the item`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25.3(1) the annual report is required to include the item` MEANS
    IF item EQUALS `s 25.3(1) another item`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "an annual report for the previous year that includes"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:711 | Limitation
-- src:712 | (2) The annual report shall not contain any information the disclosure of which would
-- src:713 | (a) compromise or hinder an ongoing investigation of an offence under an Act of Parliament;
-- src:714 | (b) compromise the identity of a public officer acting in an undercover capacity, of a confidential informant or of a person acting covertly under the direction and control of a public officer;
-- src:715 | (c) endanger the life or safety of any person;
-- src:716 | (d) prejudice a legal proceeding; or
-- src:717 | (e) otherwise be contrary to the public interest.
@ref s 25.3(2) (src:711-717)
DECLARE `s 25.3(2) disclosure of the information would` IS ONE OF
    `s 25.3(2)(a) compromise or hinder an ongoing investigation of an offence under an Act of Parliament`
    `s 25.3(2)(b) compromise the identity of a public officer acting in an undercover capacity, of a confidential informant or of a person acting covertly under the direction and control of a public officer`
    `s 25.3(2)(c) endanger the life or safety of any person`
    `s 25.3(2)(d) prejudice a legal proceeding`
    `s 25.3(2)(e) otherwise be contrary to the public interest`
    `s 25.3(2) none of those`

@ref s 25.3(2) (src:711-717)
GIVEN effect IS A `s 25.3(2) disclosure of the information would`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25.3(2) the annual report is barred from containing the information` MEANS
    IF effect EQUALS `s 25.3(2) none of those`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (2) names five effects of disclosure and says nothing of information whose disclosure would have none of them
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 25.4 -- Written notification to be given`

-- src:718 | Written notification to be given
-- src:719 | 25.4 (1) When a public officer commits an act or omission — or directs the commission by another person of an act or omission — under paragraph 25.1(9)(a) or (b), the senior official with whom the public officer files a written report under section 25.2 shall, as soon as is feasible after the report is filed, and no later than one year after the commission of the act or omission, notify in writing any person whose property was lost or seriously damaged as a result of the act or omission.
@ref s 25.4(1) (src:718-719)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 25.2 the person who bears the duty` `s 25.2 the act the duty is to do`
`s 25.4(1) the duty of the senior official to notify in writing the person whose property was lost or seriously damaged` MEANS
    PARTY `s 25.2 a senior official`
    MUST `s 25.4 notify in writing the person whose property was lost or seriously damaged`
    WITHIN 1   -- years, from the commission of the act or omission: "no later than one year after the commission of the act or omission"
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the senior official did not notify in writing, no later than one year after the commission of the act or omission, the person whose property was lost or seriously damaged"

@ref s 25.4(1) (src:718-719)
GIVEN `a public officer commits an act or omission, or directs the commission by another person of an act or omission, under paragraph 25.1(9)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the senior official has the public officer's written report under section 25.2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's property was lost or seriously damaged as a result of the act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25.4(1) the senior official is required to notify the person in writing` MEANS
    IF `a public officer commits an act or omission, or directs the commission by another person of an act or omission, under paragraph 25.1(9)(a) or (b)`
       AND `the senior official has the public officer's written report under section 25.2`
       AND `the person's property was lost or seriously damaged as a result of the act or omission`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "notify in writing any person whose property was lost or seriously damaged as a result of the act or omission"

@ref s 25.4(1) (src:719-719)
GIVEN `the day of the commission of the act or omission` IS A DATE
      `the day the senior official notified the person in writing` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25.4(1) the notification is no later than one year after the commission` MEANS
    IF `the day the senior official notified the person in writing` AT MOST `add years` `the day of the commission of the act or omission` 1
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no later than one year after the commission of the act or omission"

-- src:720 | Limitation
-- src:721 | (2) The competent authority may authorize the senior official not to notify the person under subsection (1) until the competent authority is of the opinion that notification would not
-- src:722 | (a) compromise or hinder an ongoing investigation of an offence under an Act of Parliament;
-- src:723 | (b) compromise the identity of a public officer acting in an undercover capacity, of a confidential informant or of a person acting covertly under the direction and control of a public officer;
-- src:724 | (c) endanger the life or safety of any person;
-- src:725 | (d) prejudice a legal proceeding; or
-- src:726 | (e) otherwise be contrary to the public interest.
@ref s 25.4(2) (src:720-726)
GIVEN `the person acting is the competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the competent authority is of the opinion that notification would not compromise or hinder an ongoing investigation, compromise the identity of a public officer, informant or covert person, endanger the life or safety of any person, prejudice a legal proceeding or otherwise be contrary to the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25.4(2) the competent authority may authorize the senior official not to notify the person yet` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person acting is the competent authority` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The competent authority may authorize the senior official"
        IF `the competent authority is of the opinion that notification would not compromise or hinder an ongoing investigation, compromise the identity of a public officer, informant or covert person, endanger the life or safety of any person, prejudice a legal proceeding or otherwise be contrary to the public interest` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not to notify the person under subsection (1) until the competent authority is of the opinion that notification would not"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 25.1(6), last sentence -- the senior official shall without delay notify the competent authority`

-- src:669 | The senior official shall without delay notify the competent authority of the designation.
@ref s 25.1(6) notify the competent authority (src:669-669)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 25.2 the person who bears the duty` `s 25.2 the act the duty is to do`
`s 25.1(6) the duty of the senior official to notify the competent authority of the designation` MEANS
    PARTY `s 25.2 a senior official`
    MUST `s 25.1(6) notify the competent authority of the designation`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the senior official did not notify the competent authority of the designation without delay"
